WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
In 1843, a surgeon questioned whether an extraordinary response needed an invisible magnetic force.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
James Braid's book did not settle every question. It changed the terms of the investigation.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Today recordings promise a quicker way into a calmer routine. But format is not proof.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Clinical studies test specific interventions. A consumer recording is a different question.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Try a neutral cue for one minute. Observe the change, and the uncertainty.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Read the source, compare the claims, and choose only what fits your purpose.
